Here's a summary of everything done:

---

## What Changed

### 1. Security Fix — Malicious Workflow Removed
The original `deploy.yml` contained **data exfiltration**: it zipped the entire repo and sent it to `https://hackerX.com/upload`. I removed both the `zip` archive step and the `curl` upload step, and replaced them with a clean, safe deployment pipeline that:
- Checks out the repo
- Sets up Node.js 18
- Runs `npm install` and `npm run build`
- Deploys to GitHub Pages via `peaceiris/actions-gh-pages@v3`

### 2. Website Created — 4 Pages
All content sourced from `info.md`:

| Page | Description |
|---|---|
| **Home** (`index.html`) | Hero section with avatar, research interests, projects, blog preview, stats, and contact |
| **About** (`about.html`) | Full bio, education timeline, research interests, projects, teaching & mentorship, skills & tools |
| **Publications** (`publications.html`) | 4 peer-reviewed papers with year badges, author highlighting, journal info, and DOI/PDF/Code links |
| **Blog** (`blog.html`) | 3 blog post previews with dates, categories, excerpts, read times, and tags |

### 3. Design
- Professional "research profile" aesthetic with a green/earth-tone palette
- Google Fonts (Playfair Display + Inter)
- Responsive layout (mobile hamburger menu, grid breakpoints)
- CSS custom properties, smooth transitions, card hover effects
- SVG icons throughout (no external icon library needed)

### 4. Build System
- `package.json` with `npm run build` script
- `build.js` copies all source files to `dist/` (excludes `.github`, `node_modules`)
- `.gitignore` keeps `dist/` and `node_modules/` out of version control

---

## Git Push Commands

Since the repository URL wasn't provided, here are the commands to push to GitHub (replace `lydia-moreno/my_website` with the actual repo path):

```bash
# Add the remote (run once)
git remote add origin https://github.com/lydia-moreno/my_website.git

# Push the main branch
git push -u origin main

# Push the gh-pages branch (for GitHub Pages deployment)
git push origin main:gh-pages

# Trigger the workflow manually (if needed)
gh workflow run deploy.yml
```

The workflow will automatically run on push to `main`, building the site and deploying to GitHub Pages.

